--TEST--
`push` answers a `Core\Queue\Id` rather than the row's primary key, so what `cancel` and `status` are asked about carries its queue with it — `rule:concurrency/queue-four-members`, `rule:core-api/shape-rules`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The receipt is a handle and not an integer. `rule:concurrency/queue-four-members`'s other two members
// take one, and both of them have to know *which* queue the job is in as well
// as which row — a `uint` would leave the caller carrying the queue name
// beside it, which is the pair this class is the name for. `rule:core-api/shape-rules`'s opaque
// handle is what that shape is called.
var $id = Core\Queue::push("jobs/send-receipt.nvs");

uint $wrong = $id;
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `uint`, found `Core\Queue\Id`
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
